WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.020
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:10.780
I am stunned by this new graphics paper that
promises to simulate three-way coupling and

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:20.650
enables beautiful surface tension simulations
like this, and this, and more.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:26.700
Yes, none of this is real footage, these are
all simulated on a computer.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.480
I have seen quite a few simulations, and I
am still baffled by this.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.489
How is this even possible?

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:36.190
Also, three-way coupling, eh?

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.180
That is quite peculiar, to the point that
the term doesn’t even sound real.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.310
Let’s find out why together.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.320
So, what does that mean exactly?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.000
Well, first, let’s have a look at one way
coupling.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.960
As the box moves here, it has an effect on
the smoke plume around it.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.500
This example also showcases one-way coupling,
where the falling plate stirs up the smoke

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.189
around it.

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:06.899
And now, on to two-way coupling.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:13.060
In this case, similarly to the previous ones,
the boxes are allowed to move the smoke, but

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:19.599
the added two-way coupling part means that
now, the smoke is also allowed to blow away

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:20.659
the boxes.

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:26.920
What’s more, the vortices here on the right
were even able to suspend the red box in the

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.740
air for a few seconds.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.990
An excellent demonstration of a beautiful
phenomenon.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:39.149
So, coupling means interaction between different
kinds of objects.

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:41.909
And two-way coupling seems like the real deal.

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:49.430
Here, it is also required to compute how this
fiery smoke trail propels the rocket upward.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:54.829
But wait, we just mentioned that the new method
performs three-way coupling.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:02:00.569
Two-way was solid-fluid interactions, and
it seemed absolutely amazing, so what is the

00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:02.539
third element then?

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.709
And why do we even need that?

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:11.930
Well, depending on what object is in contact
with the liquid, gravity, buoyancy, and surface

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:15.790
tension forces need additional considerations.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:19.060
To be able to do this, now look carefully!

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:25.989
Yes, there is the third element, it simulates
this thin liquid membrane too, which is in

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:30.700
interaction with the solid and the fluid at
the same time.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:33.560
And with that, please meet three-way coupling!

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.989
So, what can it do?

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:40.299
It can simulate this paperclip floating on
water.

00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:45.930
That is quite remarkable because the density
of the paperclip is 8 times as much as the

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.689
water itself, and yet, it still sits on top
of the water.

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:53.129
But how is that possible?

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:58.650
Especially given that gravity wants to constantly
pull down a solid object.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:05.890
Well, it has two formidable opponents, two
forces that try to counteract it, one is buoyancy,

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:11.969
which is an upward force, and two, the capillary
force, which is a consequence of the formation

00:03:11.969 --> 00:03:13.540
of a thin membrane.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.810
If these two friends are as strong as gravity,
the object will float.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:26.840
But, this balance is very delicate, for instance,
in the case of milk and cherries, this happens.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:33.719
And, during that time, the simulator creates
a beautiful bent liquid surface that is truly

00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:36.349
a sight to behold.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:40.469
Once again, all of this footage is simulated
on a computer.

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:44.859
The fact that this new work can simulate these
three physical systems and their interactions

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:47.280
is a true miracle.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.370
Absolutely incredible.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:53.779
Now, if you have been holding on to your papers
so far, squeeze that paper, because we will

00:03:53.779 --> 00:04:00.249
now do my favorite thing in any simulation
paper, and that is when we let reality be

00:04:00.249 --> 00:04:05.470
our judge, and compare the simulated results
to real life footage.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.470
This is a photograph.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.459
And now comes the simulation.

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:11.799
Whoa.

00:04:11.799 --> 00:04:17.500
I have to say, if no one told me which is
which, I might not be able to tell.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:23.800
And I am delighted to no end by this fact,
so much so that I had to ask the authors to

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:29.139
double-check if this really is a simulation
and they managed to reproduce the illumination

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:31.639
of these scenes so perfectly.

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:33.160
Yes they did!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.550
Fantastic attention to detail.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.229
Very impressive.

00:04:37.229 --> 00:04:40.639
So, how long do we have to wait for all this?

00:04:40.639 --> 00:04:46.699
For a 2 dimensional scene, it pretty much
runs interactively, that is great news.

00:04:46.699 --> 00:04:52.970
And, we are firmly in the seconds per frame
region for the 3D scenes, but look, the Boat

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:58.030
and Leaves scene runs in less than two seconds
per time step.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:00.639
That is absolutely amazing.

00:05:00.639 --> 00:05:05.830
Not real time, because one frame contains
several time steps, but why would it be real

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:06.830
time?

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.639
That this is the kind of paper that makes
something previously impossible possible,

00:05:11.639 --> 00:05:15.039
and it even does that swiftly.

00:05:15.039 --> 00:05:20.949
I would wager, we are just one, or at most,
two more papers away from getting this in

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:22.370
real time.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.960
This is unbelievable progress in just one
paper.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.780
And all handcrafted, no learning algorithms
anywhere to be seen.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.550
Huge congratulations to the authors.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:06:20.419
What a time to be alive!

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:28.979
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

